-- FG circuit pilot S2s: port of Tools.ShippingChildComposeA onto the context-predicate bundles (RefLawsAOpsX / RefLawsATeleX); generated by a rename-only script (names + suffix X, `AdmCtx O.quiet` -> `O.adm`). No sorry/axiom/native_decide/TRUSTED/law.

/-! # The JQ depth induction with the handler premises discharged inside each depth step

`bodyStepA_of_handlersX` (FrontCP) asks `∀ D, LegacyImplAX O (JQ O.quiet D)` up front — but the
legacy body's proof (`legacyImplA_of_teleX`, unit B) needs `ChildEntryAX O (JQ O.quiet D)`, which
holds only under the step's own hypothesis `ChildKeepsAX O D`. So the handlers are NOT assumed at
every depth here: inside the step at `D`, from `hC : ChildKeepsAX O D`,

    hC ─(D2 bridge childEntryA_JQ_of_childSynthAX)→ ChildEntryAX O (JQ D)
       ─(B legacyImplA_of_teleX, with A canonKeyAX, T)→ LegacyImplAX O (JQ D)
       ─(A legacyCachedA_of_implX)→ LegacyCachedAX O (JQ D);  C projFieldNameAX T → ProjFieldNameAX
       ─(D bodyKeepsA_frontendsX, with LegacyTailAX)→ BodyKeepsAX O D.

This file states only that STEP, with `LegacyTailAX O D` as an argument. The induction
(`childKeepsA_allX`, DepthA) and the tail itself (built from the same `hC` by B3
`legacyTailA_of_stepX`) are in Tools/ShippingChildMainA.lean, whose `core_tripleA_main` has no tail
premise. NOT here: the child-cache invariant (`JQC`, unit E), runtime fit of the laws, the model→ST
correspondence (open). -/

namespace Tools.ShippingChildComposeA
open Lean Meta
open Tools.ShippingEntrySoundness
open Sparkle.Compiler.Elab
open Tools.ShippingChildInv
open Tools.ShippingChildInvA
open Tools.ShippingChildFresh
